### MCP over Streamable HTTP, stateless session mode.
### Base address is the local API (loopback only, bearer auth required).
### Sign in at /api/v1/auth/login and send the token below.

@base = https://localhost:5208/mcp

### 1. Handshake. The server answers with its capabilities and the
### negotiated protocol version. Stateless mode keeps no session, so no
### session id comes back and every request stands alone.

POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2025-11-25",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": { "name": "mcp-http-smoke", "version": "1.0.0" }
  }
}

### 2. Tool list. Expect all 13 tools: get_health, list_sources,
### list_sessions, get_session, list_profiles, get_profile,
### create_profile, update_profile, list_runs, get_run,
### list_run_postings, start_run, cancel_run.

POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

### 3. Liveness call. Read-only and infallible by contract; proves the
### handler pipeline resolves behind the transport.

POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": { "name": "get_health", "arguments": {} }
}
